 * same instruction kept in force — it names the roles it binds and the tickets
 * it covers, and it keeps binding them on every later turn until the manager
 * explicitly lifts it.
 *
 * It is deliberately not part of `RestaurantState`: that contract is
 * schema-locked and published (see contracts/restaurant-arena-state-*.json).
 * Directives live in the engine's own replay state instead, read through
